Shard Language Syntax
=====================

This document describes the proposed syntax for Shard. It is a reference
draft; implementation details may change as the language develops.

Lexical conventions
-------------------

Statements end with a semicolon. Braces delimit blocks. Identifiers begin with
a letter or underscore and may contain letters, digits, and underscores.

// Single-line comment \\

//
   Multi-line comment
\\

Modules
-------

#include ("math");
#from ("math") include ("sqrt");

Functions
---------

Function parameters use a type followed by a name. The return type is inferred
from the returned value in this draft.

def greet(str name) {
    return "Hello, " + name;
}

def add(int left, int right) {
    return left + right;
}

Variables and types
-------------------

Supported types in this draft are int, float, bool, str, and char.

int item_count = 10;
float temperature = 21.5;
bool is_ready = true;
str city = "Reykjavik";
char initial = 'R';

Control flow
------------

if (item_count > 0) {
    print(item_count);
} elif (item_count == 0) {
    print("No items");
} else {
    print("Invalid count");
}

while (item_count > 0) {
    item_count--;
}

for (value in values) {
    print(value);
}

for (index in range(0, 10)) {
    print(index);
}

break and continue may be used inside loops.

Pattern matching
----------------

Each case ends with a semicolon-terminated statement. Cases do not fall through.

match (status_code) {
    case 200:
        print("Success");
    case 404:
        print("Not found");
    default:
        print("Unexpected status");
}

Expressions and input
---------------------

Expressions follow conventional arithmetic precedence. Function calls use
parentheses, and input is requested by specifying the expected type.

float celsius = input(float);
float fahrenheit = (celsius * 9 / 5) + 32;
print(fahrenheit);

Formatted strings use f-prefixed string literals. Expressions inside braces
are evaluated and converted to strings.

print(f"{celsius} degrees Celsius is {fahrenheit} degrees Fahrenheit.");